*.tar.gz

# ── Secrets ──
# .local/ holds credentials.key, the AES-256-GCM master key that every stored
# integration secret (Shodan, VirusTotal, Jira, webhook signing keys) is
# encrypted with. The previous entry read ".local.claude/", which matched
# nothing — the key was one `git add .` away from being published.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.local/
*.pem
*.key

# ── Logs and runtime output ──
*.log
server-run.err
pg.log
push-out.txt

# ── Test and build artifacts ──
test-results/
playwright-report/
playwright-results.xml
coverage/
tests/e2e/.auth-state.json
.playwright-mcp/

# ── Generated reports and scan output ──
# Customer scan data and rendered reports; these are outputs, not source.
*.docx
*.pdf
/*.png
/*-scan.json
/live-findings.json

# Working captures and scan reports that show REAL customer data.
#
# `.gitignore` already says scan output is "outputs, not source", but its globs
# only covered the repo root and docx/pdf — so a rendered .md report and 40
# UI captures of a live customer workspace were one `git add .` from a public
# remote. `capture-ui.mjs` deliberately picks the workspace with the MOST
# findings, which is by definition a real estate, and the captures name its
# hosts, IPs and unremediated weaknesses.
#
# The screenshots README publishes are deliberately of hackthissite.org, a
# legal CTF target, and are committed by name. Anything else here is working
# evidence: keep it local.
/*-osint-easm-report.md
/*-report.md
docs/screenshots/*
!docs/screenshots/login.png
!docs/screenshots/dashboard-overview.png
!docs/screenshots/dashboard-stats.png
